/**
 * The `secure` project: the default deployment, with secure mode on.
 *
 * There is nothing here but the layer list, on purpose — `flags/secure-mode` is
 * the same fragment an operator layers with `npm run up -- default flags/secure-mode`,
 * so what this project tests and what a deployment can actually be composed into
 * are one thing rather than two copies.
 *
 * `base/core` + `data/synthetic-dzi` is the data half of the `synthetic` project
 * (`test/env/synthetic.json`), so this differs from it by the flag. That matters
 * more here than tidiness: a project that also changed which plugins load, or
 * which slide protocol is default, could not attribute a failure to `secureMode`.
 * The slide is the generated one because no project may depend on an image
 * server it does not start itself.
 *
 * `secureMode` is reachable only from a deployment: it lives at
 * `core.client.<active_client>.secureMode`, reaches the client as
 * `APPLICATION_CONTEXT.secureMode` via `ENV.client.secureMode` (`src/app.ts`),
 * and is deliberately absent from the `setup` block so the boot sanitizer drops
 * any attempt to set it from a session bundle or URL params.
 */
{
  "$base": ["base/core", "data/synthetic-dzi", "flags/secure-mode"]
}
